              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When you're running routes across Florida or pushing beyond state lines, your tires do more than carry weight. They protect your uptime, your fuel efficiency, and your bottom line.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Choosing the best semi truck tires isn't about chasing the cheapest option or the most aggressive tread. It's about reliability over thousands of miles, especially in a state known for extreme heat, sudden storms, and long highway stretches.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we work with owner-operators and fleet managers every day who are balancing tire performance, replacement schedules, and maintenance costs. Understanding what truly matters can help you avoid premature wear, unexpected blowouts, and downtime that costs more than the tires themselves.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-florida-conditions",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Makes the Best Semi Truck Tires for Florida Conditions?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "florida-conditions"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-florida-conditions-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Florida trucking presents unique challenges that demand smarter tire choices. Heat, humidity, and high-speed interstate driving all accelerate wear if the wrong tire is used.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-florida-conditions-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Heat Resistance Matters More Than You Think",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-florida-conditions-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "High pavement temperatures soften rubber compounds, increasing wear and raising the risk of tire failure. That's why the best semi truck tires for Florida are engineered with heat-resistant compounds designed to hold their structure under sustained highway speeds.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-florida-conditions-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "According to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, tire-related issues account for a significant portion of roadside breakdowns for commercial vehicles, many linked to heat and under-inflation. Choosing tires rated for regional conditions helps reduce those risks.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-florida-conditions-5",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Match Tires to Your Driving Style",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-florida-conditions-6",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all tires are built for the same workload. Long-haul truck tires are designed for steady interstate speeds, focusing on even tread wear and fuel efficiency. Regional or mixed-service tires may offer better traction but wear faster under constant highway use. Ask yourself:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-florida-conditions-7",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Are most of your miles highway or stop-and-go?"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Do you frequently haul heavy or uneven loads?"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Are you running consistent routes or variable terrain?"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-florida-conditions-8",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "These answers help determine which commercial truck tires deliver the best return over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-tire-maintenance",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Semi Truck Tire Maintenance: The Key to Long-Term Value",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "tire-maintenance"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-tire-maintenance-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Even the best tire won't perform well without proper care. Semi truck tire maintenance is often overlooked until a problem shows up, and by then, it's expensive.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-tire-maintenance-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Maintenance Practices That Extend Tire Life",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-tire-maintenance-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Consistent pressure checks to prevent uneven wear"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Proper alignment to avoid shoulder damage"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Regular rotation for balanced tread life"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Visual inspections for early signs of damage"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-tire-maintenance-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The U.S. Department of Energy notes that proper tire inflation alone can improve fuel efficiency by up to 3%, which adds up quickly over long distances. If you're unsure whether your current tires are wearing correctly, stop by Sun State International's Parts Department for expert guidance and trusted tire options built for your routes.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-to-choose-the-best-semi-truck-tires-for-long-term-hauls/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State International technician inspecting a semi truck's front axle and tire"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-tire-replacement",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When Is Semi Truck Tire Replacement the Right Call?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "tire-replacement"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-tire-replacement-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Delaying semi truck tire replacement might seem like a cost-saving move, but it often leads to higher expenses down the road. Tires with worn tread, sidewall damage, or uneven wear increase stopping distances and reduce fuel efficiency. Signs it's time to replace include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-tire-replacement-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Tread depth below legal limits"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Frequent air pressure loss"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Visible cracking or bulging"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Vibration or pulling while driving"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-tire-replacement-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Replacing tires proactively helps prevent roadside breakdowns and keeps your operation moving on schedule.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-tire-replacement-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-tire-replacement-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
